# CDN/trusted proxy IP list
# Format: one IP/CIDR per line, lines starting with # are comments
# Supports: IPv4 CIDR, IPv6 CIDR, wildcards (192.168.*), exact IPs
# This file is hot-reloaded (checked every 10s via mtime), no restart needed
#
# When trust_proxy_headers="on" and this file exists:
#   Only trust XFF/X-Real-IP when remote_addr matches an IP in this file.
# When this file is absent: trusts XFF from any source (original behavior).
# When this file exists but all lines are commented/empty: trusts XFF from any source
#   (same as absent — falls back to original behavior, safe to keep an empty file).
#
# <<< TIP >>>
# This file ships with ALL entries commented out.
# As-is, it behaves the same as if the file doesn't exist (trusts all XFF).
# To enable CDN IP verification, uncomment or add your CDN/proxy IPs below.
# Without any active entries, XFF is trusted from any source (original behavior).
#
# Find your CDN's IP ranges from their official documentation:
#   Cloudflare:  https://www.cloudflare.com/ips/
#   AWS CloudFront: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/LocationsOfEdgeServers.html
#   Akamai:      https://developer.akamai.com/cli/apps/akamai-cli-list-ip
#   Aliyun CDN:  https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/27134.html
#   Tencent CDN: https://cloud.tencent.com/document/product/228/52935
#
# --- Example: Cloudflare IPv4 ---
#173.245.48.0/20
#103.21.244.0/22
#103.22.200.0/22
#103.31.4.0/22
#141.101.64.0/18
#108.162.192.0/18
#190.93.240.0/20
#188.114.96.0/20
#197.234.240.0/22
#198.41.128.0/17
#162.158.0.0/15
#104.16.0.0/13
#104.24.0.0/14
#172.64.0.0/13
#
# --- Example: Cloudflare IPv6 ---
#2400:cb00::/32
#2606:4700::/32
#2803:f800::/32
#2405:b500::/32
#2405:8100::/32
#2a06:98c0::/29
#2c0f:f248::/29
